  "reason": "Existing single-profile RNA results show scvi_n200 is the strongest RNA encoder (0.520 accuracy, 0.498 F1), while PCA and scGPT are weaker and ResNet50 image-only is weak. The main uncertainty is whether multiprofile aggregation can improve the best RNA representation. config_005 extends config_004 by adding multiprofile with simple avgpool, isolating the profile/aggregation effect without adding fusion or a transformer. This is the best next experiment because it tests an important design choice on the strongest RNA encoder, may improve performance directly, and will clarify whether more complex aggregation or multimodal fusion is worth testing next."
